      "id": "efc2d589-9556-4710-a5a3-7842e3b13146",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "#### CTIS 210 Project 2\n\nThis project focuses on the work we've done in the following two activities.\n\n* Kinds of Numbers and Arithmetic Operators\n* Data Types\n\nYou will use the following concepts from previous projects and activities.\n\n* Declaring and initializing variables\n    * That includes using an appropriate type and identifier\n* Assigning a new value to a variable\n\nYou will do the following in this project.\n\n* Use arithmetic operators to perform mathematical operations\n* Manipulate strings using operators that act on a `String` object\n* Read text information from the user that can be used as text or converted into numbers\n* Investigate how a color can be represented in Java\n* Draw some objects with colors you specify",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "efc2d589-9556-4710-a5a3-7842e3b13146"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "43f60fcf-6b25-4a51-a8a4-e0c06c69e285",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "##### One item before you start\n\nLook at the top of this window and find the buttons named\n\n* Clear All Outputs\n* Restart\n\nWhenever working on a notebook, if you run into a place where you want to have all the code run again from the very beginning, click those two buttons in order. You'll need to confirm the Restart.\n\nIf you still have problems after doing that, commit and sync your notebook and email me with a description of what's not working.",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "43f60fcf-6b25-4a51-a8a4-e0c06c69e285"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "33558d51-805d-4d02-bb2c-374759eea153",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "##### Task: Variable declaration\n\nIn the code cell below, declare the following variables using the correct type and the specified integer. Just declare them; don't initialize them\n\n* A `String` variable with an identifier appropriate for storing your G number.\n* Three integer variables with the following identifiers\n    * `firstTwo`\n    * `secondTwo`\n    * `thirdTwo`\n* Three integer variables with the following identifiers\n    * `red`\n    * `green`\n    * `blue`\n",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "33558d51-805d-4d02-bb2c-374759eea153"
      }
    },
